IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Schedule 1 -- Meaning of commonly used words and expressions: the table of defined terms.
-- One entry for every defined term, in the order the schedule prints them, with the wording of its definition and its text as printed (lines of the text joined with " / ").
-- An entry whose text shows only the term and three dots is a term the text shows blank.

§ `Schedule 1 -- the defined terms`

DECLARE `Kind of wording of a definition` IS ONE OF
    means
    includes
    `means and includes`
    `has the meaning given by`
    `has the same meaning as`
    see
    is
    `by paragraphs`
    `blank in this text`

DECLARE `Schedule 1 entry` HAS
    term IS A STRING
    wording IS A `Kind of wording of a definition`
    text IS A STRING
    `first line` IS A NUMBER
    `last line` IS A NUMBER


