GIVEN term IS A STRING
      entries IS A LIST OF `Schedule 1 entry`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Schedule 1 entry`
`the first entry in the list for the term` MEANS
    CONSIDER entries
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF e's term EQUALS term
        THEN JUST e
        ELSE `the first entry in the list for the term` term rest

GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Schedule 1 entry`
`the entry of schedule 1 for the term` MEANS
    `the first entry in the list for the term` term `all the entries of schedule 1`

GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of wording of a definition`
`the wording of the definition of the term in schedule 1` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entry of schedule 1 for the term` term
    WHEN JUST e THEN JUST (e's wording)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the first line of the entry of the term in schedule 1` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entry of schedule 1 for the term` term
    WHEN JUST e THEN JUST (e's `first line`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 36(1): "a term defined in schedule 1 has the meaning stated in that schedule".  A term the schedule lists but shows blank has no meaning stated; a term it does not list is not answered.
GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the term is defined in schedule 1` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entry of schedule 1 for the term` term
    WHEN JUST e THEN
        CONSIDER e's wording
        WHEN `blank in this text` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
